WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:15.340
Short and sweet review number five. We discussed a situation where a person accidentally did the terrible sin of washing a dirty milk utensil in a fleshig meat sink with dirty meat utensils. Terrible, terrible situation.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:22.140
Well, we said even though it's so terrible, all the utensils can still be considered permitted for numerous reasons.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.700
First of all, we know that the water coming out of the sink possibly was not a yad soledes bo.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:31.280
Maybe it was below Yat Salat Yisbo, temperature, in which case it would not make any effect on the kelim, on the utensils.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:36.240
Also, we mentioned there were shitas who hold, the opinions that hold that maybe a faucet has a status of iri klisheni,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.160
which for sure does not transfer any flavor, even if it has iri klisheni on there,

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.960
Rama holds that that cannot forbid dishes as well.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.520
We mentioned that most people use soap. Soap works as a po-game.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:50.260
It ruins the flavor of the meat or dairy residue and stops any issues from taking place.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:56.300
And we have the groundbreaking chiddish of Rav Moshe Feinstein that held that if as long as there was a little bit of cold water on,

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.560
Shulchan Aruch

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:53.880
Shulchan Aruch

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.600
POSKIM

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:31.260
and Dairy, for sure not using them together, but even if you would use the same dishwasher for meat

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:36.220
and then dairy dishes one after the next, it's still not something that the Ashkenazi Kiposkin

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:41.020
were okay with. First of all, they said that even though soap is used in a dishwasher, it's only

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:47.080
added later in the cycle, and first there is a non-soap cycle, which does give flavor. Second of

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:51.040
all, there are many times food particles, if they're stuck in the filter or in crevices, and those food

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.040
particles can make problems in contact, if they're in contact with the wrong type of utensil. And

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:02.560
And third of all, since the heating element is inside of the dishwasher, it might actually make the water mamisha klirishon,

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:07.640
which would, and you would not get the same allowances of a sink, of maybe being a klisheni.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:14.120
However, the Sephardic posts were more lenient, and they allowed using the dishwashers for meat and then dairy,

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:18.220
Rav Ovadya even allowed using them together, again, assuming that the initial rinse cycle is cold.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.460
There are many factors why the Sephardim are more make-all and more lenient.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:25.700
First of all, they said even if the dishwasher is a klirishon, it's only iri klirishon,

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.520
They also are a fan of the soap being po-game.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:35.860
And also, third of all, they say it's very unlikely that particles will become in contact with the dishes in a way that will be posing a problem.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.060
In summary, though, there are many differences between how dishwashers work.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.700
You have to know how your dishwasher works.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.640
You have to then ask a Rav for guidance.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:48.100
And then before a person uses the same dishwasher for both meat and dairy dishes.
